/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 650.50 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 639.00 Tm (1. `Rover.cpp` gets the active HAL with `AP_HAL::get_HAL\(\)`.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 627.50 Tm (2. In a Linux build, `AP_HAL::get_HAL\(\)` returns the global `HAL_Linux hal_linux` ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 616.00 Tm (object.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 604.50 Tm (3. `HAL_Linux` constructs the generic `AP_HAL::HAL` base class and passes ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 593.00 Tm (`&schedulerInstance` into it.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 581.50 Tm (4. The base `AP_HAL::HAL` stores that pointer as `hal.scheduler`.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 570.00 Tm (5. `AP_HAL_MAIN_CALLBACKS\(&rover\)` creates `main\(\)` and calls `hal.run\(argc, argv, ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 558.50 Tm (&rover\)`.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 547.00 Tm (6. Because `hal` is really `HAL_Linux`, that calls `HAL_Linux::run\(\)`.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 535.50 Tm (7. `HAL_Linux::run\(\)` calls `scheduler->init\(\)` and ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 524.00 Tm (`scheduler->set_system_initialized\(\)`.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 512.50 Tm (8. Those virtual calls dispatch to methods implemented in ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 501.00 Tm (`AP_HAL_Linux/Scheduler.cpp`.) Tj
