/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 667.50 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 656.00 Tm (That `scheduler.loop\(\)` is the `AP_Scheduler` vehicle-task scheduler. It eventually ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 644.50 Tm (runs tasks selected from `Rover::scheduler_tasks[]`.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 633.00 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 621.50 Tm () Tj
/F2 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 618.50 Tm (AP_HAL_Linux::Scheduler) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 607.00 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 595.50 Tm (Defined in `ardupilot/libraries/AP_HAL_Linux/Scheduler.cpp`. This is the Linux ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 584.00 Tm (platform scheduler. It handles Linux threads, delays, timer callbacks, IO callbacks, ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 572.50 Tm (failsafe callbacks, and realtime scheduling setup.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 561.00 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 549.50 Tm (The two are related but not the same object. Rover's `AP_Scheduler` runs vehicle ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 538.00 Tm (tasks. The Linux HAL scheduler provides the platform timing and threading services ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 526.50 Tm (underneath it.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 515.00 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 503.50 Tm () Tj
/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 499.50 Tm (Direct Uses From Rover Code) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 483.50 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 472.00 Tm (Rover and common vehicle code can call the HAL scheduler directly through ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 460.50 Tm (`hal.scheduler`, for example:) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 449.00 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 437.50 Tm () Tj
/F3 7.3 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 432.50 Tm (hal.scheduler->register_timer_failsafe\(failsafe_check_static, 1000\);) Tj
/F3 7.3 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 423.70 Tm (hal.scheduler->delay\(100\);) Tj
/F3 7.3 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 414.90 Tm (hal.scheduler->is_system_initialized\(\);) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 406.10 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 401.10 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 389.60 Tm (On Linux, these calls dispatch to `Linux::Scheduler` methods in ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 378.10 Tm (`AP_HAL_Linux/Scheduler.cpp`.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 366.60 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 355.10 Tm () Tj
/F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 351.10 Tm (Summary) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 335.10 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 323.60 Tm (`Rover.cpp` links to `AP_HAL_Linux/Scheduler.cpp` through object construction and ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 312.10 Tm (virtual calls, not through a direct include. The build selects the Linux HAL, ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 300.60 Tm (`AP_HAL::get_HAL\(\)` returns `hal_linux`, `HAL_Linux` installs `Linux::Scheduler` as ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 289.10 Tm (`hal.scheduler`, and the generic Rover code reaches Linux scheduler behavior through ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 277.60 Tm (`hal.run\(\)` and `hal.scheduler->...` calls.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 266.10 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 254.60 Tm (There is no separate `Rover::loop\(\)` in `Rover.cpp`. The generated `main\(\)` passes ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 243.10 Tm (`&rover` as an `AP_HAL::HAL::Callbacks` object, `HAL_Linux::run\(\)` calls ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 231.60 Tm (`callbacks->loop\(\)`, and that dispatches to `AP_Vehicle::loop\(\)`. From there, ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 220.10 Tm (`AP_Scheduler::loop\(\)` runs Rover's task table.) Tj
ET
